Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:00:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Witness rebound worker loss in modern failure
 recovery

A restart receipt becomes unattributable after a continued worker binds. If that worker dies before recording its own result, the diagnostic worker_lost cannot satisfy strict recovery and modern evidence vetoes expiry forever. Capture a causal loss receipt at the owner write, retain unknown exit status and all historical death fences, and let dispatcher/observer book one crash. Existing legacy losses stay legacy; later bindings/results and damaged receipts hold. RED: both observer/dispatcher restart-rebind-loss tests retain running. GREEN: 1471 tests across nine focused/guard suites; new regression controls 8 passed. Live incident and five-whys: t_01a1d76bb38f3504.
